    "role": "assistant",
    "content": "{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Improve memory locality and loop order by using a blocked approach to process submatrices in larger chunks.\",\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Reorganize the nested loops to ensure better cache utilization by processing blocks of the matrix together.\",\n    \"Adjust the block size dynamically based on the input matrix size for optimal performance.\"\n  ],\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\",\n      \"content\": \"#include <iostream>\\n#include <vector>\\n#include <cstdio>\\n#include <cassert>\\n#include <climits>\\n\\nint main() {\\n\\tint n, s;\\n\\tstd::cin >> n >> s;\\n\\tstd::vector<std::vector<int>> matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\\n\\tfor (int i = 0; i < n; i++)\\n\\t\\tfor (int j = 0; j < n; j++) \\n\\t\\t\\tscanf(\\\"%d\\\", &(matrix[i][j]));\\n\\n\\tassert(s < n);\\n\\tassert(n < 8000);\\n\\tassert(s > 0);\\n\\tassert(n > 0);\\n\\n\\tint blockSize = std::min(32, s); // Define a block size for better cache utilization\\n\\tint mxSum = INT_MIN;\\n\\n\\tfor (int bi = 0; bi < n - s + 1; bi += blockSize) {\\n\\t\\tfor (int bj = 0; bj < n - s + 1; bj += blockSize) {\\n\\t\\t\\tint sum = 0;\\n\\t\\t\\tfor (int i = bi; i < std::min(bi + blockSize, n - s + 1); i++) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tfor (int j = bj; j < std::min(bj + blockSize, n - s + 1); j++) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tsum += matrix[i][j];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\tmxSum = std::max(mxSum, sum);\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tfor (int i = bi; i < n - s + 1; i++) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif (i > bi) { // Slide the block down by one row\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tfor (int j = bj; j < std::min(bj + blockSize, n - s + 1); j++) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tsum -= matrix[i - s][j];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif (i + s < n) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tsum += matrix[i][j];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tfor (int j = bj; j < n - s + 1; j++) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif (j > bj) { // Slide the block right by one column\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tsum -= matrix[i][j - s];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tif (j + s < n) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tsum += matrix[i][j];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tmxSum = std::max(mxSum, sum);\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tprintf(\\\"%d\\\\n\\\", mxSum);\\n}\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"Adjusted the block size to be dynamically determined based on the submatrix size 's' and ensured that the sliding window technique processes blocks efficiently within the bounds of the matrix.\"\n}"
